AWPTCM-T30142 (1.0)  portauth auth-mac - unauthorised port blocks
Run date : 2026-09-09      Bench : tb470 (IE520)
Software : IE520-awplus_main-20260905-1714.rel  (AlliedWare Plus, build 09/04/26; bootloader pauld)
Result   : PASS
================================================================================

RESULT
  A port with auth-mac enabled BLOCKS all data while the host is unauthenticated, and
  FORWARDS once the host's MAC is authenticated.  Verified for:
      packets to the device system MAC ... BLOCKED  (ping to u4 SVI: 100% loss)
      unicast / broadcast (ARP) .......... BLOCKED  (ping across port to u5: 100% loss)
      DLF (unknown-unicast) .............. BLOCKED  (no flood to u5)
      L2 multicast (snooping off) ........ BLOCKED  (no egress to u5)
  Control (same wiring, MAC now authenticated): ALL of the above FORWARD, 0% loss.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BENCH / TOPOLOGY AS TESTED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  DUT / authenticator : u4  S/N 264A23052  MAC 84e3.2787.09c0
  Supplicant / host   : tb470 eth2  MAC 00:f0:4d:00:77:17,  10.10.60.20/27
                        -> u4 port1.0.2  (access vlan60, auth-mac enabled)
  Egress observer     : u5  S/N 264A23066,  vlan60 SVI 10.10.60.3, reached only via the
                        u4<->u5 vlan60 trunk (u4 port1.0.24 <-> u5 port2.0.24).
  RADIUS              : the IE520's own on-box local RADIUS server (no external server).

METHOD / SCOPE
  No IXIA / supplicant software needed. "Unauthenticated" = the host MAC is NOT a user in
  the local RADIUS DB, so auth-mac's Access-Request is rejected and the port stays blocked.
  The host injects each packet type with scapy and pings; "blocked" is proven by 100% ping
  loss AND by u5 (the only other port in vlan60) never learning the host MAC or ARP. The
  control authenticates the exact same MAC by adding it to the RADIUS DB. Functional test.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG APPLIED   (running-config only, NOT saved to startup)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
u4#
  radius-server local
   server enable
   nas 127.0.0.1 key localkey
  radius-server host 127.0.0.1 key localkey
  aaa authentication auth-mac default group radius
  vlan 60  (name authtest);  interface vlan60  ip address 10.10.60.1/27 ; no ip igmp snooping
  interface port1.0.2
   switchport mode access
   switchport access vlan 60
   auth-mac enable
  interface port1.0.24
   switchport trunk allowed vlan add 60      (span vlan60 to u5 for egress observation)

u4# show radius local-server statistics
 Server status      : Run (administrative status is enable)
 Enabled methods    : MAC EAP-MD5 EAP-TLS EAP-PEAP

